Files: application/include/common/rolling_list.h
Copyright: 1991-2025 Linus Torvalds and others
           2003 Kazutomo Yoshii <kazutomo@mcs.anl.gov>
Comment:
 Derived from the Linux kernel include/linux/list.h, which is GPL-2.  This is
 the only file in the package that is not under LGPL-2.1.
 .
 LGPL-2.1 section 3 allows a work that uses this library to be relicensed
 under the GNU GPL version 2, which is how the binaries that include this
 header are distributed.  rolling_list.h is header-only and is compiled into
 rolling_helper and into the two service archives, so those binaries are
 effectively GPL-2 as a whole; every other source file is LGPL-2.1.
License: GPL-2

Files: binary_deb/*
Copyright: 2025-2026 Rolling Wireless S.a.r.l.
License: Rolling-binary-1.0
Comment:
 The four prebuilt static archives (libcode.a, libmtk_rw350r_dell_2.0.25.a,
 librolling_config_service_2.0.11.a, librolling_flash_service_2.0.19.a)
 redistributed with the permission of the copyright holder.  The services
 link against them, so the package cannot be built without them.
 .
 This repository publishes only the service entry points (rolling_config_main.c,
 rolling_flash_main.c, rolling_helper_main.c), the headers and the
 D-Bus/systemd/udev integration; the translation units compiled into these
 archives (rolling_config_parse.c, rolling_flash_update.c,
 rolling_helper_adapter.c, ... -- 24 in total) are not published here, so the
 archives cannot be rebuilt from this source package and do not satisfy the
 Debian Free Software Guidelines requirement that the preferred form for
 modification be available.  Redistribution itself is granted by SECTION B of
 the top-level LICENSE file, and a self-contained copy of that grant ships
 next to the archives as binary_deb/common_lib/LICENSE.

Files: application/rolling_ma_service/*
Copyright: 2025-2026 Rolling Wireless S.a.r.l.
License: Rolling-binary-1.0
Comment:
 rolling_ma, the ModemManager FCC-unlock helper, is shipped as a prebuilt
 x86-64 executable.  The sources it was built from (rolling_ma_main.c,
 rolling_ma_at.c, sha256.c, dmidecode.c) are not published and this directory
 contains no CMakeLists.txt, so nothing here is compiled from source; the
 binary does not meet DFSG 2 either.
 .
 rolling_ma incorporates dmidecode-derived code, which is GPL-2 by its
 original authors; SECTION B item 5 commits the copyright holder to providing
 that source on written request.  A self-contained copy of the grant ships
 next to the binary as application/rolling_ma_service/LICENSE.

